# One system track as the goat-processors runner publishes it: one JSON
# object per line of its tracks output (goat-processors runner/README.md,
# "What the runner publishes"). Public, no external standard. `system` is
# the system track's identifier when correlate makes the tracks, `group` when
# fuse does (the runner writes one of them), `track_number` its number 1 to
# 65535 held while the track lives, `mono` 1 when its members come from one
# source and 0 when from more, and `now_ms` the tick it describes.
format  goat-processors-system-track
version 0.4.0
distribution public
source  "USAREUR-AF/goat-processors runner/README.md, section What the runner publishes (Apache-2.0)"
uses    track
uses    cat062
uses    radar
wire    json
field   uid       group     string
field   cat062.track_number  track_number  int
field   time_ms   now_ms    int
field   lat       lat       float
field   lon       lon       float
field   hae       hae       float
field   course    course    float
field   speed_ms  speed_ms  float
field   type      attributes.type.value      string
field   callsign  attributes.callsign.value  string
field   cat062.mon  mono      int
field   radar.rcs_m2  rcs_m2  float
